Ported code
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/model.rs re-implements, on burn, the inference path of VITS as Piper trains and exports it:
  - VITS, "Conditional Variational Autoencoder with Adversarial Learning for End-to-End Text-to-Speech"
    https://github.com/jaywalnut310/vits  (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 Jaehyeon Kim)
    models.py (TextEncoder, StochasticDurationPredictor, ResidualCouplingBlock, Generator), attentions.py
    (relative-position multi-head attention), modules.py (DDSConv, WN, ConvFlow, ResBlock2, ElementwiseAffine),
    transforms.py (the rational-quadratic spline, ported in rq_spline_inverse).
  - Piper (the MIT-licensed original, not piper1-gpl)
    https://github.com/rhasspy/piper  (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2022 Michael Hansen)
    src/python/piper_train/vits (the training copy of VITS whose ONNX export this crate mirrors) and the phoneme id
    layout (^ _ p _ ... $) used by Speaker::phoneme_ids.
No code from OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl (piper-tts >= 1.3, GPL) is used, in the crate or in its test tools.

